# Test fixtures under crush/tests/fixtures/ are checked byte-for-byte against
# SHA-256 hashes in checksums.json (see crush/tests/conftest.py's
# pytest_configure fixture-corpus integrity check). Any line-ending
# conversion (e.g. Windows CI's default core.autocrlf=true rewriting LF to
# CRLF on checkout) changes those bytes and fails the check for text-typed
# fixtures (.json/.cpp/.md/.js) even though nothing was actually tampered
# with -- so every fixture, text or binary, must be left untouched on
# checkout regardless of platform.
crush/tests/fixtures/** -text
